  "releaseNotes": "- [ThunderPropagator#54] [Background Workers] IterativeFeeder — error-backoff delay uses StartAsync CancellationToken instead of ApplicationStopping; app shutdown blocked during backoff [Major]   src/ThunderPropagator.Application/Feeders/IterativeFeeder.cs (line 113–116):   - The backoff Task.Delay now uses a CancellationTokenSource.CreateLinkedTokenSource combining both cancellationToken (from StartAsync) and applicationLifetime.ApplicationStopping. Previously it   only used applicationLifetime.ApplicationStopping directly (no combined token). The using var ensures the linked CTS is disposed after each backoff iteration.",
